---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Sources & Methodology | CivicConnect" description="Learn about the government datasets, acts, and verification methods used by CivicConnect.">
  <div class="container section max-w-4xl">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-16">
      <span class="badge badge-soft mb-3" data-tone="accent">Data Governance</span>
      <h1 class="text-h1 mb-4">
        Sources & Methodology. <span class="text-muted-foreground">Rigorous statutory grounding.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        How CivicConnect ingests, indexes, verifies, and presents Indian legislation and citizen welfare aid.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Content Sections -->
    <div class="space-y-10">
      
      <article class="card space-y-4">
        <span class="badge badge-soft" data-tone="primary">Authoritative Repositories</span>
        <h2 class="text-h2 text-2xl">Official Document Sources</h2>
        <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          CivicConnect utilizes publicly available government databases. Rather than scraping uncontrolled web sources, we curate and index verified PDF documents and HTML resources directly from primary statutory sources:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-small text-muted-foreground">
          <li><strong>The Gazette of India:</strong> The official public journal carrying newly enacted central acts such as the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita 2023 and the Motor Vehicles Act 1988.</li>
          <li><strong>State Government Gazettes:</strong> Gazette publications from states like Maharashtra, providing state-specific legislative modifications and pensions.</li>
          <li><strong>National Government Services Portal (services.india.gov.in):</strong> Official records of central and state citizen welfare eligibility details.</li>
          <li><strong>Individual Ministry Portals:</strong> Direct operational manuals and gazette notifications from the Ministry of Agriculture, Ministry of Health and Family Welfare, and others.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="card space-y-4">
        <span class="badge badge-soft" data-tone="accent">Pipeline Engineering</span>
        <h2 class="text-h2 text-2xl">Hybrid Retrieval & Context-Constrained Synthesis</h2>
        <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          When you write a question in the assistant, the backend does not rely on raw LLM parameters:
        </p>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3 text-small text-muted-foreground">
          <li>
            <strong>Hybrid Dense & BM25 Search:</strong> The system matches question terms against the indexed statutory database using reciprocal rank fusion (RRF) to isolate exact relevant sections and clauses.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Jurisdiction Filtering:</strong> Matches your chosen jurisdiction (Central or State) to exclude irrelevant legislation.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Context-Closed Synthesis:</strong> The isolated statutory clauses are formatted into a constrained prompt. The AI reasoning engine is instructed to cite only the retrieved facts and decline to answer if sources are not found.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </article>

      <article class="card space-y-4">
        <span class="badge badge-soft" data-tone="warning">Corpus Constraints</span>
        <h2 class="text-h2 text-2xl">Currency & Coverage Limitations</h2>
        <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          CivicConnect outputs reflect the indexed files in the database:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-small text-muted-foreground">
          <li><strong>Update Schedule:</strong> Government guidelines and thresholds can be updated by ministries. We run regular ingestion syncs, but always cross-verify high-consequence deadlines with the official Gazette.</li>
          <li><strong>Expanding Coverage:</strong> The statutory database is continuously expanding to cover additional state regulations and municipal bylaws.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
